From f0ce904788f8acab63ff424045f470d6eba00309 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pratik Pachange <ppachang@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 14:43:54 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] qtimlqnn: Add support for HTP DCVS performance modes

Add a "htp-performance-mode" property to qtimlqnn exposing the
standard QNN HTP DCVS performance profiles matching the settings
documented for each mode in the QNN HTP backend guide. The engine
retrieves the HTP perf infrastructure via
QnnDevice_getInfrastructure() and applies the selected mode through
a DcvsV3 power config after device creation; backends that don't
expose the perf interface are left unaffected.

Change-Id: I8a4c9083a81116fed67086888f1ee434c0e70d29
Signed-off-by: Pratik Pachange <ppachang@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Raja Ganapathi Busam <rbusam@qti.qualcomm.com>
